// Bindings for the deployed Cloudflare worker.
//
// Nitro reads this file at build time and merges it into the wrangler.json it
// writes to .output/server/, so this is the one place a service is attached to
// the worker. Nothing in it is needed to run the app locally.
//
// The worker has no writable disk, so it has no way to keep an account alive
// across a restart without a binding of some kind. This one is a Workers KV
// namespace: a key/value store inside the same Cloudflare account as the
// worker, created with the same CLI. No second vendor, no key, no separate bill.
// An account is one JSON value under `u:<name>` — there is no schema and no SQL
// to it, which is the closest a Worker gets to a text file.
//
// To turn it on:
//   1. npx wrangler kv namespace create muis   (prints a namespace id)
//   2. paste that id below and delete the "//" markers
//   3. deploy
//
// Without it the worker answers exactly as it always has: it reports accounts as
// unavailable, and everything that does not need an account keeps working.
{
  // "kv_namespaces": [
  //   {
  //     "binding": "MUIS",
  //     "id": "PASTE_THE_NAMESPACE_ID_HERE"
  //   }
  // ]
}
